ll":"B5","value":1029176.48,"formula":null,"unit":"USD"},{"sheet":"Cash","cell":"B6","value":97318.4,"formula":null,"unit":"USD"},{"sheet":"Cash","cell":"B7","value":250000.0,"formula":null,"unit":"USD"},{"sheet":"E03 Cash Position","cell":"C2","value":1029176.48,"formula":null,"unit":"USD","source":"02 Cash/Cash Position - November 2, 2026.xlsx","sha256":"0390b4be5f673b0029786ef4b1769a5a167db5b8b6ccb656795105127e1e2561","locator":"Cash Position!C2"},{"sheet":"E03 Cash Position","cell":"C3","value":97318.4,"formula":null,"unit":"USD","source":"02 Cash/Cash Position - November 2, 2026.xlsx","sha256":"0390b4be5f673b0029786ef4b1769a5a167db5b8b6ccb656795105127e1e2561","locator":"Cash Position!C3"},{"sheet":"E03 Cash Position","cell":"C5","value":250000,"formula":null,"unit":"USD","source":"02 Cash/Cash Position - November 2, 2026.xlsx","sha256":"0390b4be5f673b0029786ef4b1769a5a167db5b8b6ccb656795105127e1e2561","locator":"Cash Position!C5"},{"sheet":"E11 Payment Procedures","cell":"D14","value":"Keep at least $250,000.00 in the operating account after committed payroll. Expected receipts are not cash. The Controller and the CFO approve each run over $100,000.00 before release; the batch is prepared for them and never released by its preparer.","formula":null,"unit":"text","source":"07 Procedures/HANGS Payment Procedures v2.1.docx","sha256":"2f3e2e44938317d3d30b8723075d8b523f5fa5bc0a6d3a9a82952cffdaebcd76","locator":"Clauses PAY-1 to PAY-8"}]}],"sources":[{"source":"01 AP Aging/AP Aging - November 2, 2026.xlsx","locator":"Open Bills sheet: every approved open bill at November 2, with terms and due date; Aging Summary sheet","sha256":"dc3c807fbf8cc8f64ab23534acba950beb4915479ba28352663401004f2f5035","name":"E01 AP Aging","originalSheet":"Open Bills","kind":"aging","moneyColumns":[6,10,11]},{"source":"01 AP Aging/AP Aging - November 2, 2026.xlsx","locator":"Open Bills sheet: every approved open bill at November 2, with terms and due date; Aging Summary sheet","sha256":"dc3c807fbf8cc8f64ab23534acba950beb4915479ba28352663401004f2f5035","name":"E02 Aging Summary","originalSheet":"Aging Summary","kind":"aging","moneyColumns":[2]},{"source":"02 Cash/Cash Position - November 2, 2026.xlsx","locator":"Cash Position sheet: the October bank reconciliation's adjusted book balance, committed payroll, expected receipts, minimum","sha256":"0390b4be5f673b0029786ef4b1769a5a167db5b8b6ccb656795105127e1e2561","name":"E03 Cash Position","originalSheet":"Cash Position","kind":"cash","moneyColumns":[2]},{"source":"03 Discounts/Early-Pay Discounts - November 2026.xlsx","locator":"Vendor Terms and Offers sheets: discount terms and the early-pay offers received","sha256":"73d066b08c56f33300adf92cfd771f90e6d669e254bff503e736e68e6a4c5019","name":"E04 Vendor Terms","originalSheet":"Vendor Terms","kind":"discounts","moneyColumns":[]},{"source":"03 Discounts/Early-Pay Discounts - November 2026.xlsx","locator":"Vendor Terms and Offers sheets: discount terms and the early-pay offers received","sha256":"73d066b08c56f33300adf92cfd771f90e6d669e254bff503e736e68e6a4c5019","name":"E05 Early-Pay Offers","originalSheet":"Offers","kind":"discounts","moneyColumns":[]},{"source":"04 Payment History/Vendor Payments - July to October 2026.xlsx","locator":"Payments sheet: vendor checks and wires since July, as recorded and as the bank cleared them","sha256":"f5925a18a912968ac7a7eac610869c07ae43091c23a9e0729e9d9db78b804c59","name":"E06 Payment History","originalSheet":"Payments","kind":"history","moneyColumns":[6,8]},{"source":"05 Vendors/Vendor Master - November 2, 2026.xlsx","locator":"Vendors sheet: terms, pay method, bank details, call-back verification, W-9, 1099 and lien waiver flags; Change Log","sha256":"6cbe1841f9d0154b57a8d6e69095dc8d466a17702ff0a69c66ce772ed2cc94ba","name":"E07 Vendor Master","originalSheet":"Vendors","kind":"vendors","moneyColumns":[]},{"source":"05 Vendors/Vendor Master - November 2, 2026.xlsx","locator":"Vendors sheet: terms, pay method, bank details, call-back verification, W-9, 1099 and lien waiver flags; Change Log","sha256":"6cbe1841f9d0154b57a8d6e69095dc8d466a17702ff0a69c66ce772ed2cc94ba","name":"E08 Vendor Change Log","originalSheet":"Change Log","kind":"vendors","moneyColumns":[]},{"source":"06 Holds/Holds and Lien Waivers - November 2, 2026.xlsx","locator":"Holds sheet: holds set in the AP system; Lien Waivers sheet: conditional waivers received by invoice","sha256":"006c646c2f45af687596edf3f1b4f259b56ed7898681ed99a071e7961d318ae9","name":"E09 Holds","originalSheet":"Holds","kind":"holds","moneyColumns":[4]},{"source":"06 Holds/Holds and Lien Waivers - November 2, 2026.xlsx","locator":"Holds sheet: holds set in the AP system; Lien Waivers sheet: conditional waivers received by invoice","sha256":"006c646c2f45af687596edf3f1b4f259b56ed7898681ed99a071e7961d318ae9","name":"E10 Lien Waivers","originalSheet":"Lien Waivers","kind":"holds","moneyColumns":[3]},{"source":"05 Vendors/Bank Change Request - Marrow Lane Electric.pdf","locator":"Page 1","sha256":"14d71839dcf57122c8a934c9dad4c39954609fad7d95419d03b9f4b2c96ef2aa","name":"BCR Page 1","originalSheet":null,"kind":"bankchange","moneyColumns":[]},{"source":"07 Procedures/HANGS Payment Procedures v2.1.docx","locator":"Clauses PAY-1 to PAY-8","sha256":"2f3e2e44938317d3d30b8723075d8b523f5fa5bc0a6d3a9a82952cffdaebcd76","name":"E11 Payment Procedures","originalSheet":null,"kind":"procedures","moneyColumns":[]}],"openItems":[{"id":"Duplicate Bill AP-10419 · PAY-3","status":"open","amount":"14615.00","explanation":"AP-10419 (BPW 5188) is AP-10409 (BPW-5188) entered a second time. Both bills are Bluepine Concrete Works, both are $14,615.00, and both invoice numbers read BPW5188 by letters and digits: 'BPW-5188' entered October 10 and 'BPW 5188' entered October 21. AP-10409 is paid in this run; AP-10419 is not. The October AP review flagged the same pair (DUP-1); void AP-10419 in the AP system."},{"id":"Already Paid QBP-3069 · PAY-3","status":"open","amount":"27.00","explanation":"QBP-3069 shows $27.00 open, but check 10431 cleared for the full $7,385.20. The aging carries QBP-3069 at $7,385.20 less $7,358.20 paid, leaving $27.00. Check 10431 was recorded as $7,358.20, but the bank cleared it on October 21 for $7,385.20, the whole invoice. The open $27.00 is a recording error, not a debt: the October bank reconciliation found the check recorded short and proposed the correcting entry. Do not pay it; post that entry and the bill closes."},{"id":"Bank Change Not Verified MLE-1401 · PAY-4","status":"open","amount":"8800.00","explanation":"Marrow Lane Electric would be paid by ACH to an account changed on October 29 that no one has called to verify. On October 28, 2026 an email asked that Marrow Lane Electric be paid by ACH to Ridgeway Federal Credit Union, account ending 7731, and Riley Chen entered it in the vendor master the next day. The call-back is not recorded. The request came from accounts@marrowlane-pay.example, not the marrowlane.example address on file, gave a phone number, (555) 019-7713, that is not the (555) 013-2280 on file, and asked not to be called. Hold MLE-1401 ($8,800.00, due November 5). Someone other than Riley Chen calls (555) 013-2280; until then nothing is paid to Marrow Lane Electric."},{"id":"Disputed Invoice KRE-2207 · PAY-7","status":"open","amount":"78117.00","explanation":"KRE-2207 from Kestrel Ridge Equipment is in dispute and stays unpaid. KRE-2207 for $78,117.00 was due November 4. Delivery billed at $1,950.00; the signed quote included delivery. Credit memo requested October 12. The hold, placed by Riley Chen on October 12, has not been released, so the whole invoice waits. When the credit memo arrives, pay the corrected amount in the next run."},{"id":"Billed to Another Entity WLC-0388 · PAY-7","status":"open","amount":"3860.00","explanation":"WLC-0388 is HANGS Property Holdings LLC's bill and is not paid from this account. WLC-0388 for $3,860.00, due November 9, is on hold: Billed to HANGS Property Holdings LLC; reclass and pay from that entity (October AP review, ENT-1). A bill addressed to another HANGS entity is paid by that entity only. Reclass it and pay it from HANGS Property Holdings LLC."},{"id":"Lien Waiver Missing SWR-8133 · PAY-6","status":"open","amount":"14300.00","explanation":"No conditional lien waiver from Stonewick Roofing for SWR-8133. Stonewick Roofing is a subcontractor. SWR-8133 for $14,300.00 is due November 7, but the lien waiver log has no conditional waiver for it (Requested October 9 and October 23; not received). Paying without one leaves HANGS exposed to a lien on the buildings if the subcontractor's own suppliers go unpaid. Hold the payment until the waiver is on file."},{"id":"Discount Lapsed QBP-3077 · PAY-2","status":"open","amount":"84.60","explanation":"The 1.00% discount on QBP-3077 closed November 2, before Thursday's release. Quarry Bend Plumbing allows 1% 10, Net 30. Invoice QBP-3077 is dated October 23, so its $84.60 discount had to be paid by November 2. With no run released on October 29, it was lost. The bill is not due until November 22 and waits for a later run. Note it for the vendor file."},{"id":"Approve the Batch · PAY-8","status":"open","amount":"136003.00","explanation":"7 payments for 11 bills, $136,003.00, wait for the Controller and the CFO. The batch is over $100,000.00, so the Controller and the CFO approve it before anything is released. Cash covers it: $681,858.08 is available after payroll and the $250,000.00 minimum, leaving $545,855.08 to spare. Nothing has been paid or released."}],"incomplete":true,"research":null}